# BPB Website — project

## Stack

- Static site on **GitHub Pages**
- **Supabase** for database + item image Storage
- Vanilla HTML/JS + **Tailwind** (page-specific) + shared/theme CSS
- Shared UI in `js/shared/`; page scripts in `js/pages/<page>/`

## Folder layout

```text
BPBWebsite/
  index.html
  builds/<slug>/index.html
  js/
    shared/
      nav.js                 # site nav — imported by every page entry
      footer.js              # site footer — imported by every page entry
      tooltip.js
      skeleton.js            # parchment loading bars/blocks
      …
    pages/<page>/index.js    # + section modules
  css/
    theme.css                # how the site looks (tokens, atmosphere)
    shared.css               # optional shared layout helpers (not nav/footer markup)
  assets/fonts/
  assets/icons/
  docs/
  .env
```

Page-specific look: **Tailwind in the HTML** (or small page helpers).  
Global look: `theme.css` (+ optional `shared.css`).  
**Nav + footer:** `js/shared/nav.js` and `js/shared/footer.js` — each page `index.js` imports and mounts them.  
Complex widgets (tooltip): module CSS next to the JS.

## JavaScript rules

- **Max ~500 lines per `.js` file** — split earlier if a file is doing multiple jobs
- Each file = **one page section or one feature** (not a dumping ground)
- Related modules live in a **folder** together (don’t leave `mod1.js`/`mod2.js` loose at repo root)
- Every page has **`js/pages/<page>/index.js`** as the home/entry file that imports and starts the other modules for that page
- The HTML page loads **only that `index.js`** (module script), not every section file individually
- Shared code stays in `js/shared/` — including **`nav.js`** and **`footer.js`**; every page entry imports and mounts them
- Pages import from shared — never copy-paste nav/footer markup into each HTML file

Example:

```html
<script type="module" src="/js/pages/home/index.js"></script>
```

```js
// js/pages/home/index.js
import { initNav } from '../../shared/nav.js';
import { initFooter } from '../../shared/footer.js';
import { initFeaturedOp } from './featured-op.js';

initNav();
initFooter();
initFeaturedOp();
```

Detail also in `docs/file-structure.md`.

## Architecture rules

- **Data-driven UI**: store item/build facts in Supabase; render with shared components
- **Never** ship one HTML file per item
- **Never** store finished tooltip HTML in the database
- Schema source of truth: `docs/db/tables.md` and `docs/db/tables/*`
- Table create order: `items` → combinations → `builds` → `build_placements` → `profiles`

## Do not

- Commit `.env` or secrets
- Recreate throwaway `_poc-assets` research dumps in the repo
- Duplicate item stats onto builds/placements/recipes
- Put page-specific logic in `js/shared/`
